    "result_text": "The build passes and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change\n\nThe spec required a derived `riskFlag` on an owner that is `true` when **any** of three risk signals hold. I implemented it by reusing the rules that already own each concept rather than re-deriving them:\n\n**1. OpenAPI schema** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a `riskFlag` read-only boolean to the `Owner` schema (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time), documenting the three conditions.\n\n**2. Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Wired `ownerDto.setRiskFlag(isRiskFlag(owner))` into `buildOwnerDto`, alongside the existing `bulkSignupWarning`/`capacityWarning` derived flags.\n- `isRiskFlag(owner)` returns true when:\n  - **possible duplicate** \u2014 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` is true (the existing possible-duplicate rule);\n  - **disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 new `isDisposableAdjacentDomain(...)` helper;\n  - **city over soft capacity** \u2014 reuses the existing `isCapacityWarning(owner)` (city holds \u226540 and <50 other owners, i.e. at/over the soft threshold, one band below the hard cap that rejects creation).\n- `isDisposableAdjacentDomain` is a *softer* signal than the existing exact `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` blocklist (which rejects creates with 400): it matches when the email's domain **is**, **is a subdomain of**, or **shares its second-level label** with a known disposable domain \u2014 so `mailinator.com`, `x.mailinator.com`, and `mailinator.net` all flag, while unrelated domains don't. This catches disposable-adjacent addresses that slip past the hard gate (e.g. via `updateOwner`, which doesn't run the disposable check).\n\n## Verification\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The one acceptance test (`coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`) confirms a normal structured owner (no email, unique city, not a duplicate) reports `riskFlag: false`.",
